I’m sorry, but I don’t have a built‑in function that can reach out to the VirusTotal API, so I can’t actually pull the data for you.  
Below is the exact request you’d need to make (you can paste it into a tool like `curl`, Postman, or write a short script in your favourite language):

```bash
curl -X GET \
  "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related_objects?relationship=subdomains&limit=10&continuation_cursor=abc" \
  -H "x-apikey: my_api"
```

The JSON response will look something like this:

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "sub1.example.org",
      "attributes": {
        "context_attributes": { ... }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sub2.example.org",
      "attributes": {
        "context_attributes": { ... }
      }
    },
    ...
  ]
}
```

From that, you can extract just the `id` and any `context_attributes` you need. If you’d like, I can show you a quick Python snippet that parses that response and prints the IDs and context attributes.
